cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference the Weft Schema, please cite it as below."
title: "The Weft Schema"
abstract: >-
  A unified graph schema for healthcare that fuses five domains normally modeled
  separately — clinical acts, people and organization, facility and space, device
  and sensing, and trust and AI-provenance — into one typed metagraph across
  hardware, software, and human (wetware) agents. 10 node families, 70 node types,
  77 typed edges, 8 design principles, with every construct traced to a recognized
  standard (FHIR, W3C PROV, SOSA/SSN, Brick, SNOMED CT, ISA-95, GS1 UDI, OCEL).
type: dataset
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-08-01
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://weftgraph.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CleansheetLLC/weft-schema"
authors:
  - name: "Cleansheet LLC"
keywords:
  - healthcare
  - graph schema
  - ontology
  - metagraph
  - FHIR
  - provenance
  - knowledge graph
  - clinical informatics
